Q: PHP switch statements for mixing scalars and objects A: <p>PHP 8 introduces the match grammar (<a href="https://www.php.net/manual/en/control-structures.match.php" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://www.php.net/manual/en/control-structures.match.php</a>):</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>$output = match (true) {
    $result === 1 =&gt; &quot;Active&quot;,
    $result instanceof User =&gt; &quot;User: &quot; . $result-&gt;name,
    default =&gt; &quot;Unknown&quot;,
};
</code></pre>
<p><code>switch(true):...</code> previously eliminated type juggling concerns:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>switch (true) {
    case $myIntegerOrComplexObject === 1:
        //$myIntegerOrComplexObject is 1 (not true)
        break;
    case $myIntegerOrComplexObject === 0:
        //$myIntegerOrComplexObject is the natural number 0 (not null)
        break;
    // Check if the result is a specific Object type
    case $myIntegerOrComplexObject instanceof User:
        //$myIntegerOrComplexObject is a type of User
        break;
    default:
        //raise exception
        break;
}
</code></pre>

Q: Get value of submit button in `onSubmit` eventhandler in React A: <pre><code>&lt;form onSubmit={(event) =&gt; { console.log(event.nativeEvent.submitter) }}&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>React gives you access to the underlying native event that has all the normal properties of <code>SubmitEvent</code>.</p>
